{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3129","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3129","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3129\",\"parent_revision\":\"a601f777ace3f87cdd99a3ceef5478c61c4865a50d2e0f59e2dd9e41c4f699e8\",\"root_revision\":\"a601f777ace3f87cdd99a3ceef5478c61c4865a50d2e0f59e2dd9e41c4f699e8\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-22\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nA worktree-isolated agent's Bash/Read/Write/Edit tool calls are NOT confined to its assigned worktree \u2014 they can freely read and write files in the shared main checkout \u2014 while its git commands (git add/git commit) ARE confined and refuse to target the shared checkout, by design. Observed directly during this session: a subagent dispatched with isolation='worktree' whose assigned worktree was on a stale branch (git could not check out the target branch there, since it was already checked out in the shared checkout) fell back to editing 5 test files directly in the shared checkout via Bash/Write, successfully, and only failed when it later tried to git-commit those same edits from that path (blocked with: 'a worktree-isolated agent's git operations must target its own worktree'). Impact: the file-write half of worktree isolation does not enforce the same boundary as the git half, so a worktree-isolated agent can silently collide with concurrent edits in the shared checkout \u2014 the exact race worktree isolation exists to prevent \u2014 as long as it only uses non-git tools to do it. Distinct from the already-filed worktree-vanishing and Bash-cwd-reset bugs (#3117/#3118): this is about the isolation boundary itself being inconsistently enforced across tool types, not about a worktree disappearing.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer relying on this plugin**, I want to **worktree isolation confines git commands to the assigned worktree but not bash/read/write file access to the shared checkout** so that **the tool works correctly and reliably**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session observation - gate_token removal work, 2026-08-22\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-22\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"8926d3e3cb1b1296bc6ccf6edaee49b2c9ca299f20ce3281652497d613ae4c4b\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABQKqnvg\"}"}